# Extra packages for the CUDA ISO variant; build-iso.sh --variant cuda
# appends this file to packages.x86_64 when staging the profile.
#
# nvidia-open is the prebuilt open kernel-module package for the stock
# 'linux' kernel (the proprietary 'nvidia' package was retired upstream in
# its favour; both support Turing and newer, which is also CUDA 13's floor).
# nvidia-utils is the driver userspace - build-iso.sh injects NoExtract lines
# that keep its display-only libraries out of this console-only image.
# linux-firmware-nvidia is the GPU firmware family the standard package list
# drops on purpose (see the comment there); the CUDA image has a real use
# for it.
nvidia-open
nvidia-utils
linux-firmware-nvidia
